# Environment for the Forgejo MCP server. See quadlets/forgejomcp.container.
#
# The unit publishes no port. Clients reach it through the gateway's
# /mcp/forgejo route on port 4000, so the gateway decides who can reach this
# server and this file decides what it does with what arrives.

FORGEJO_URL=(url of your Forgejo instance, e.g. https://forgejo.example.org)
# No FORGEJO_ACCESS_TOKEN here, on purpose: this server holds no Forgejo
# credential at all. Every request arrives through the gateway's /mcp/forgejo
# route carrying an Authorization header that the gateway substituted for a
# client's surrogate token, and this server forwards that header to Forgejo. The
# real token lives in installed/envars/agentgateway.env, with the provider keys
# and GITHUB_MCP_PAT -- other upstream credentials the gateway presents. Nothing
# was needed here: the server was checked against 3.4.0 and starts, and serves,
# with no token of its own (`token_configured: false`).

# Host names the server answers to, matched by host with no wildcard; a name
# missing here is a 403 on every request. An entry without a port matches any
# port, so a plain name is enough.
#
# Through the gateway the Host is the backend's own name on devnetng,
# systemd-forgejomcp, which is why that entry is the one that matters. The
# loopback names are left in for a direct container-to-container call from
# devnetng, where they cost nothing; they do NOT make the server reachable from
# the host, because nothing is published. The server logs the Host it refused, so
# a 403 names its own fix.
FORGEJO_MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=systemd-forgejomcp,localhost,127.0.0.1,[::1]

# OFF, and this file has no operator token for it to fall back to: a request
# that carries no Authorization header is refused rather than served with a
# credential. With the fallback on and no FORGEJO_ACCESS_TOKEN in this container,
# there is nothing to serve it with either -- so this is belt and braces on the
# one path that bypasses the gateway, a container on devnetng calling this
# server directly. See the gateway route for the path clients actually take.
FORGEJO_MCP_ALLOW_OPERATOR_TOKEN_FALLBACK=0
